      "manual_source_review": "main dispatches to resume_preflight or run_resume; both validate fixture/FD inputs and reconstruct the fixed four-column metric. run_resume verifies the predecessor ZIP/report/calls/replay gate, exact accepted state and objective, native/source fingerprints, then rebuilds H=G^-1 from existing accepted secants. It runs a fresh bounded native gradient at the resume point, forms and applies the pending secant, then takes bounded inverse-BFGS directions with strict actual-objective Armijo trials; every accepted endpoint is followed by a fresh gradient and secant update. Existing stage/solver and native objective sources remain unchanged. The final Red fix keeps attempted update labels separate from accepted-update ordinals, pins PR283 resume ZIP/input hashes, and treats the validated terminal-gradient or last accepted-trial objective as final-cost authority."
    },
